Based on your screenshot and requirements, the data structure in Firestore is actually on the right track, but we need to ensure the **parent user document** is created and that we aren't mixing different versions of the Firebase SDK (which causes the "blank screen" error).

### 1. The Right Data Structure
Your screenshot shows: `users (coll) -> {UID} (doc) -> accounts (sub-coll)`. 
This is **correct**. To make it perfect, we will:
*   Ensure `users/{UID}` document is created with a `name` and `email` field.
*   Organize `transactions`, `accounts`, and `goals` as sub-collections under that UID.
*   Organize `preferences` inside a `config` sub-collection.

### 2. Blank Screen Fix
The blank screen is happening because your `index.html` import map is mixing `gstatic.com` links with `esm.sh` links. This creates two conflicting versions of Firebase in the browser. I have standardized everything to one version.

### 3. Firestore Rules
You should copy and paste these into your Firebase Console under **Firestore Database > Rules**:

```javascript
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    // Allow users to read and write only their own data
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;

      // Allow access to all sub-collections (transactions, accounts, goals, config)
      match /{allSubcollections=**} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### 4. Code Updates

