To resolve the `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'indexOf')` error and ensure your user profiles sync correctly with Firestore, we need to update the security rules and make the application's data layer more resilient.

### Firestore Rules (Update these in your Firebase Console)
The previous rules matched only documents *under* the user ID, but missed the user document itself. Update them to this:

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId} {
      // Allow access to the user profile document itself
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;

      // Allow access to all subcollections recursively
      match /{allPaths=**} {
        allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Application Updates
I have updated `dataService.ts` to ensure that even if a document is partially created, the `name` field is always handled safely, and `App.tsx` now includes guards to prevent rendering components with invalid account selections or missing user data.

